IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `esl-levy`

-- Emergency Services Levy Act 2002 (WA), with Part 6A of the Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) -- the Q&A
-- layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, "Which of these describes you"): the land owner (the baseline's seat; an owner under FES Act s 3A,
-- which takes in a mortgagee in possession and a lessee or occupier of Crown land); and the tenant or occupier of land
-- someone else owns, who is not liable for the levy on freehold land but may get back levy they paid (s 36T(2)). Every
-- exported question takes `my role` first. A question about the other role answers `does not arise for you` without
-- reading any other input, so the form never asks those inputs. The Minister, the local government and the FES
-- Commissioner are never a seat: what they determine, assess or recover appears as what it means for the person.
--
-- SITUATIONS (graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's
-- fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading anything
-- else. The questions of one situation share one input, the same name, type and @desc, so the form asks it once. All
-- are BOOLEAN, and FALSE gives `does not arise for you`:
--   - `I own the land with others`: the two co-owner questions (ss 36J(3), 36P(3));
--   - `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid`: interest (s 36S), recovery (s 36Z(1)), the charge (s 36O), sale
--     (s 36ZC) and caveat (s 36ZD); for the tenant or occupier, recovery (ss 3A, 36Z(1));
--   - `the land changed owners during the levy year`: apportionment between successive owners (s 36T(1)(a));
--   - `I have objected to my levy`: the two questions that follow an objection to the purpose of use (ss 36ZE(2)(d),
--     (3), 36ZF);
--   - `I have objected to my levy or my valuation`: the three s 36ZH questions, which s 36ZH(1) and (2) apply also to
--     an objection to the valuation under the Valuation of Land Act 1978 and to a review by the Tribunal;
--   - for the tenant or occupier, `I have paid levy on land I do not own`: being paid back (s 36T(2)).
-- No question that arises in every situation of its role takes one.
--
-- For the owner, each question calls the baseline function of the same subject in esl-levy.l4 and restates no rule;
-- where its situation holds its answer is the baseline export's, carried in the answer types below. Where the
-- baseline's input is the situation itself (the co-owner, the caveat), or is settled by it (unpaid levy, for interest),
-- the layer passes TRUE. The tenant's questions call the same functions, with the interest in the land the role fixes.
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- Conventions, as in the baseline: a levy year is named by the calendar year in which it ends (2029/30 is 2030); a day
-- is written as the number YYYYMMDD; money is in dollars.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Emergency Services Levy Act 2002 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I own land in Western Australia`
    `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Day answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `on the day` HAS `the day, written YYYYMMDD` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `this many days` HAS `number of days` IS A NUMBER

-- ss 36J(4), 36L, carried: the baseline's three answers, and `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `Notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `it comes as part of your council rate notice`
    `it comes as a separate notice from your local government`
    `it comes as a notice from the FES Commissioner`

§§ `Carrying the baseline's answers, and the helpers the tenant's questions need`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `the route` IS A `How my levy notice comes`
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`the notice route, carried` `the route` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `as part of my council rate notice` THEN `it comes as part of your council rate notice`
    WHEN `as a separate notice from my local government` THEN `it comes as a separate notice from your local government`
    WHEN `as a notice from the FES Commissioner` THEN `it comes as a notice from the FES Commissioner`

-- s 3A: a lessee of Crown land, or another person with a right to occupy it, is its owner (para (a)(i)); a tenant of
-- freehold land is not (para (d) names the proprietor).
GIVEN `the land is Crown land I lease or have a right to occupy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My interest in the land`
`my interest, as a tenant or occupier` MEANS
    IF `the land is Crown land I lease or have a right to occupy`
    THEN `lessee or occupier of Crown land`
    ELSE `tenant of freehold land`

-- s 36Z(1) recovers from the owner on the day the notice was served, or a person who becomes the owner while the levy is
-- unpaid. A tenant of freehold land is neither, so nothing after the first input is read for that tenant.
GIVEN `the land is Crown land I lease or have a right to occupy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I held the land when the notice was served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I came to hold the land while the levy was unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the levy can be recovered from me as a tenant or occupier` IF
    IF `the land is Crown land I lease or have a right to occupy`
    THEN `Can unpaid levy on this land be recovered from me` `I held the land when the notice was served` `I came to hold the land while the levy was unpaid`
    ELSE FALSE

§§ `For the land owner (the baseline's seat)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (esl-levy.l4) and restates no rule: for this role,
-- and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above.

§§§ `ESL Act s 3 -- the levy imposed`

@export Does the Emergency Services Levy Act 2002 (WA) itself fix how much levy I pay (s 3; the levy is worked out under Part 6A of the Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the Emergency Services Levy Act itself fix my levy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Does the Emergency Services Levy Act itself fix how much levy I pay`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `FES Act ss 36B, 36D, 36E -- is my land leviable`

@export Does another law's exemption from rates or taxes free me from the emergency services levy (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36E)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the land` IS A `My land for the levy year` @desc Your land for the levy year
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does another law's exemption free me from the levy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Does another law exempt me from the levy` `the land`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my land leviable land, on which the emergency services levy is charged (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) ss 3, 36B, 36D, 36E)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the land` IS A `My land for the levy year` @desc Your land for the levy year
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my land leviable land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is my land leviable` `the land`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `FES Act ss 3A, 36J(3), 36P -- am I the one liable`

@export Am I an owner of the land for the emergency services levy (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 3A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my interest` IS A `My interest in the land` @desc What your interest in the land is
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an owner of the land for the emergency services levy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Am I an owner of the land` `my interest`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I liable to pay the emergency services levy on this land for the levy year (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36P(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my interest` IS A `My interest in the land` @desc What your interest in the land is
      `the land` IS A `My land for the levy year` @desc Your land for the levy year
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I liable to pay the emergency services levy on this land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Am I liable to pay the levy` `my interest` `the land`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be made to pay all of the levy on land I own with others (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36P(3): co-owners are jointly and severally liable)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I own the land with others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is owned by you and one or more others
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a co-owner, can I be made to pay all of the levy on our land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I own the land with others`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be made to pay all of the levy on land I own with others` `I own the land with others`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is a levy notice served on my co-owner taken to be served on me (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36J(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I own the land with others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is owned by you and one or more others
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is a levy notice served on my co-owner taken to be served on me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I own the land with others`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is a notice served on my co-owner served on me` `I own the land with others`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `FES Act ss 36F, 36G, 36H, 36I -- how much`

@export By what day must the levy for this levy year be determined in the Gazette (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36G)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the levy year` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy year, named by the year in which it ends (2029/30 is 2030)
      `the Minister declared another day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister declared a relevant day other than 31 May
      `the declared day` IS A NUMBER @desc The declared day, written YYYYMMDD (0 if none was declared)
GIVETH A `Day answer`
`By what day must the levy for this levy year be determined` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `on the day` (`By what day must the levy for this year be determined` `the levy year` `the Minister declared another day` `the declared day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export On which day is the gross rental value fixed that my levy is worked out on (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36H(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the levy year` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy year, named by the year in which it ends (2029/30 is 2030)
GIVETH A `Day answer`
`Which day fixes the gross rental value for my levy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `on the day` (`On which day is the gross rental value for my levy fixed` `the levy year`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much emergency services levy is charged on my land for the levy year (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) ss 36B, 36H, 36I)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the land` IS A `My land for the levy year` @desc Your land for the levy year
      `the determination` IS A `The determination for my land` @desc The Minister's Gazette determination for your land's category and use
      `the gross rental value` IS A NUMBER @desc The gross rental value of the land in force at 1 July in the levy year
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much emergency services levy is charged on my land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `amount` (`How much levy is charged on my land` `the land` `the determination` `the gross rental value`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can a change to my area's ESL category affect my levy for this levy year (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36F(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the levy year the notice was published in` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy year in which the Gazette notice was published
      `the levy year` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy year, named by the year in which it ends (2029/30 is 2030)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a change to my area's ESL category affect this levy year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Can a change to my area's category affect this year's levy` `the levy year the notice was published in` `the levy year`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `FES Act ss 36J, 36L, 36P(2) -- the notice, and whom I pay`

@export How will my emergency services levy assessment notice come to me (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) ss 36J(4), 36L)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the assessor` IS A `Who assessed my levy` @desc Who assessed the levy on your land, and served the assessment notice on you
      `my local government gives me a rate notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your council gives you a rate notice for the year
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`How will my levy assessment notice come to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `the notice route, carried` (`How will my levy notice come to me` `the assessor` `my local government gives me a rate notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I pay my emergency services levy to my local government (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36P(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the assessor` IS A `Who assessed my levy` @desc Who assessed the levy on your land, and served the assessment notice on you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I pay my emergency services levy to my local government` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Do I pay my levy to my local government` `the assessor`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `FES Act ss 36M, 36Q, 36S -- when, how, and interest`

@export At the earliest, how many days after my notice was issued can my levy fall due (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36M(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Days answer`
`At the earliest, how many days after my notice was issued can my levy fall due` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `this many days` (`How many days after my notice was issued can my levy fall due at the earliest`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my levy fall due this many days after the date my notice was issued (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36M(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the days after issue` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the issue date stated in the notice to the due date stated in it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my levy fall due this many days after my notice was issued` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Can my levy fall due this many days after issue` `the days after issue`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I pay my levy other than in one payment (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) ss 36Q, 36R(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Minister has approved instalment arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether instalment arrangements are approved for the levy
      `I have a payment agreement with my local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a payment agreement with the council
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I pay my levy in instalments or by agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`May I pay my levy other than in one payment` `the Minister has approved instalment arrangements` `I have a payment agreement with my local government`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Asked where levy has fallen due and is unpaid, so the baseline's first input is TRUE by the situation's terms.
@export Does interest run on my unpaid levy (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36S(1), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether levy, or an instalment of levy, that has fallen due on the land is still unpaid
      `I am entitled to a rebate or deferment of the levy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to a rebate or deferment under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992
      `I am of a kind prescribed as free of interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations prescribe you as a person on whom no interest accrues
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does interest run on the levy I have not paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does interest run on my unpaid levy` TRUE `I am entitled to a rebate or deferment of the levy` `I am of a kind prescribed as free of interest`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `FES Act ss 36O, 36T, 36Z -- buying, selling, and unpaid levy`

-- A levy year is "the financial year for which the levy is payable" (FES Act s 3), 1 July to 30 June, so it has 366
-- days when it takes in a 29 February, else 365.
-- The days are asked as that yes/no, so the baseline's division always has a divisor in its domain.
GIVEN `the levy year has 366 days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days in the levy year` MEANS
    IF `the levy year has 366 days` THEN 366 ELSE 365

@export The land changed owners during the levy year: what part of the year's levy is apportioned to me (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36T(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the land changed owners during the levy year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought or sold the land, or it otherwise changed owners, during the levy year
      `the levy for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy for the whole levy year
      `the days I owned the land` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of the levy year for which you owned the land
      `the levy year has 366 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the levy year has a 29 February in it, and so 366 days rather than 365
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What part of the year's levy falls to me as a successive owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `the land changed owners during the levy year`
        THEN `amount` (`What part of the year's levy is apportioned to me` `the levy for the year` `the days I owned the land` (`days in the levy year` `the levy year has 366 days`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I reimburse someone else who paid levy on my land (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36T(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone other than me paid levy on my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another person paid part of the levy on land you own
      `we agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and that person agreed that you need not reimburse
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I pay back someone else who paid levy on my land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Must I reimburse someone who paid levy on my land` `someone other than me paid levy on my land` `we agreed otherwise`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can levy left unpaid on this land be recovered from me (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36Z(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether levy, or an instalment of levy, that has fallen due on the land is still unpaid
      `I owned the land when the notice was served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the owner on the day the assessment notice was served
      `I became the owner while the levy was unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became owner later, while that levy was still unpaid
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the unpaid levy on this land be recovered from me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can unpaid levy on this land be recovered from me` `I owned the land when the notice was served` `I became the owner while the levy was unpaid`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is unpaid levy, with interest and recovery costs, a charge on my land (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36O)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether levy, or an instalment of levy, that has fallen due on the land is still unpaid
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the unpaid levy a charge on my land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is unpaid levy a charge on my land`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `FES Act ss 36ZC, 36ZD -- what can happen to my land if I do not pay`

@export Can an application be made to sell my land for unpaid levy (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36ZC(1)-(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether levy, or an instalment of levy, that has fallen due on the land is still unpaid
      `the years the levy has been unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole years the levy has been due and unpaid
      `the months since notice of the intended application` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since the newspaper notices (and your notice, if your whereabouts are known) were given
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my land be sold for unpaid levy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can an application be made to sell my land` `the years the levy has been unpaid` `the months since notice of the intended application`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The baseline's one input is the situation itself.
@export Can a caveat be lodged against my land for unpaid levy (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36ZD)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether levy, or an instalment of levy, that has fallen due on the land is still unpaid
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a caveat be lodged against my land for the unpaid levy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can a caveat be lodged against my land` `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `FES Act ss 36ZE, 36ZF, 36ZH -- objecting`

@export May I object to the purpose for which my land is taken to be used (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36ZE(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my levy depends on the purpose of use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rate or the minimum or maximum for your land differs by the purpose it is used for
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I object to the purpose my land is taken to be used for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`May I object to the purpose my land is taken to be used for` `my levy depends on the purpose of use`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Was my objection in time (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36ZE(2)(d), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have objected to my levy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have served an objection on the Minister under s 36ZE to the purpose for which your land is taken to be used
      `the days after my notice was served` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from service of the assessment notice to service of your objection on the Minister
      `the Minister extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister, on your application, extended the time far enough
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was my objection in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I have objected to my levy`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my objection in time` `the days after my notice was served` `the Minister extended the time`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I apply to the State Administrative Tribunal for review of the Minister's decision on my objection (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36ZF)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have objected to my levy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have served an objection on the Minister under s 36ZE to the purpose for which your land is taken to be used
      `I objected and the Minister has determined my objection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has decided your objection
      `I am dissatisfied with the determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are dissatisfied with the Minister's decision
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I apply to the State Administrative Tribunal for a review of the objection decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I have objected to my levy`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I apply to the State Administrative Tribunal` `I objected and the Minister has determined my objection` `I am dissatisfied with the determination`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I still pay the levy while my objection is pending (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36ZH(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have objected to my levy or my valuation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have objected to the purpose for which your land is taken to be used (s 36ZE) or to your land's valuation under the Valuation of Land Act 1978, or applied for a review of either
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I still pay the levy while my objection is decided` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I have objected to my levy or my valuation`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I still pay the levy while my objection is pending`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much is refunded to me when my levy is adjusted after my objection or review (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36ZH(3)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have objected to my levy or my valuation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have objected to the purpose for which your land is taken to be used (s 36ZE) or to your land's valuation under the Valuation of Land Act 1978, or applied for a review of either
      `what I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy you paid
      `the adjusted levy` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy as adjusted after the objection or review
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much is refunded to me when my levy is adjusted down` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I have objected to my levy or my valuation`
        THEN `amount` (`How much is refunded to me after an adjustment` `what I paid` `the adjusted levy`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For how many days after the adjustment notice am I safe from recovery of an underpayment (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36ZH(3)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have objected to my levy or my valuation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have objected to the purpose for which your land is taken to be used (s 36ZE) or to your land's valuation under the Valuation of Land Act 1978, or applied for a review of either
GIVETH A `Days answer`
`For how many days after an adjustment notice am I safe from recovery of an underpayment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I have objected to my levy or my valuation`
        THEN `this many days` (`How many days after an adjustment notice before an underpayment can be pursued`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the tenant or occupier of land someone else owns (FES Act ss 3A, 36P(1), 36T(2), 36Z(1))`

-- A tenant of freehold land is not an owner (s 3A(d)) and so is not liable for the levy (s 36P(1)); a lessee or
-- occupier of Crown land is an owner (s 3A(a)(i)). A tenant who pays levy, for example under the lease, may get it back
-- from the owner (s 36T(2)). The questions call the baseline's functions with the interest the role and the answers fix.

§§§ `FES Act ss 3A, 36P(1), 36Z(1) -- am I liable`

@export Am I liable to pay the emergency services levy on the land I rent or occupy (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) ss 3A, 36P(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the land is Crown land I lease or have a right to occupy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is Crown land, and you are its lessee or have a right to occupy it
      `the land` IS A `My land for the levy year` @desc Your land for the levy year
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I liable for the levy on the land I rent or occupy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `yes if` (`Am I liable to pay the levy` (`my interest, as a tenant or occupier` `the land is Crown land I lease or have a right to occupy`) `the land`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 36Z(1) recovers from "the owner": a tenant of freehold land is not one (s 3A(d)), so for that tenant nothing
-- else is read; a lessee or occupier of Crown land is (s 3A(a)(i)).
@export Can levy left unpaid on the land I rent or occupy be recovered from me (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) ss 3A, 36Z(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether levy, or an instalment of levy, that has fallen due on the land is still unpaid
      `the land is Crown land I lease or have a right to occupy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is Crown land, and you are its lessee or have a right to occupy it
      `I held the land when the notice was served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the lessee or occupier on the day the assessment notice was served
      `I came to hold the land while the levy was unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became the lessee or occupier later, while that levy was still unpaid
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the levy on the land I rent or occupy be recovered from me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN
        IF `levy on my land has fallen due and is unpaid`
        THEN `yes if` (`the levy can be recovered from me as a tenant or occupier` `the land is Crown land I lease or have a right to occupy` `I held the land when the notice was served` `I came to hold the land while the levy was unpaid`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `FES Act s 36T(2) -- being paid back`

-- s 36T(2) is the owner's duty to the person who paid: the baseline's function, asked from the payer's side, with
-- its first input TRUE by the situation's terms.
@export I paid levy on land I do not own: must its owner pay me back (Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA) s 36T(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have paid levy on land I do not own` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid some or all of the levy on land you do not own, for example under your lease
      `the owner and I agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the owner agreed that the owner need not pay you back, for example in your lease
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the owner pay me back the levy I paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN
        IF `I have paid levy on land I do not own`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I reimburse someone who paid levy on my land` TRUE `the owner and I agreed otherwise`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
